{
    "background_story": "Scout was a small, unassuming cankerworm moth who lived in a lush orchard. Despite her humble appearance, Scout had a big impact on the ecosystem. She spent her days flitting from branch to branch, laying eggs that would hatch into caterpillars. These caterpillars, though often viewed as pests, played a crucial role in pruning the trees and promoting healthy growth. Scout's offspring were particularly skilled at targeting weak and diseased limbs, allowing the trees to conserve energy and thrive. As the seasons passed, the orchardists came to appreciate Scout's quiet contributions, recognizing that her cankerworms were a natural and essential part of the orchard's delicate balance. Scout's story served as a reminder that even the smallest creatures can have a profound impact on the world around them.",
